    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
    </div>

    <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
        <TimeLineElement
            title="Bachelor of Science in Electrical and Computer Engineering, Minor in Computer Science"
            subtitle="University of Iowa • Expected May 2027 • GPA: 3.96/4.00"
        />
    </div>

    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
    </div>

    <div class="time-line-container mb-10">

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Hardware Engineering Co-op at Schneider Electric"
            subtitle="Jan 2026 - Present"
        >
            Design, simulate, and test PCB for driving solenoid and current sensing.
            <br/ >
            2D/3D FEA for electromagnetic solenoid design.
            <br/ >
            Write LabView programs for test automation and DSP code for data processing.
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Incomming Electromagnetic Theory Teaching Assistant at University of Iowa"
            subtitle="Aug 2026 - Dec 2026"
        >
            Host office hours and help out students with their studies in EM theory.
            <br/ >
            Assist with putting up exam questions for mid-terms and finals.
            <br/ >
            Grade exams and homeworks in a timely manner.
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Incoming Engineering Peer Advisor at University of Iowa"
            subtitle="Aug 2026 - May 2027"
        >
            Help answering students' questions regarding academic and career development.
            <br/ >
            Coordinate events with corporates in the Engineering field, to provide students' with more insights of what industry is like in reality.
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Electrical and Automation Engineering Co-op at Novelis"
            subtitle="May 2025 - Dec 2025"
        >
            Designed and implemented a plant-first Ignition-Based HMI/SCADA system to address real-time data visualization needs, enabling operators to monitor PLC performance and detect system faults 20% faster than previous methods.
            <br/ >
            Learned RSLogix software and ladder logic programming within 3 months to support Rockwell PLC-Ignition software integration requirements.
            <br/ >
            Created a comprehensive technical documentation library of 20+ guides covering troubleshooting procedures, feature implementation, and networking protocols, reducing new team member onboarding time.
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Digital Logic Design Teaching Assistant at University of Iowa"
            subtitle="Aug 2025 - Dec 2025"
        >
            Graded over 1000 homeworks and exams throughout the semester.
            <br/ >
            Held weekly office hours to help faciliate students' learning.
            <br/ >
            Led lab sessions and assisted over 200 students with circuits set-up and debugging.
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Research Assistant at Fluid Dynamics Lab at University of Iowa"
            subtitle="July 2024 - Aug 2025"
        >
            Applied advanced particle image velocimetry (PIV) techniques to capture fluid flow dynamics in synthetic jet experiments, generating critical velocity field data that contributed to 1 peer-reviewed research publications on flow control mechanisms
            <br/ >
            Developed custom MATLAB algorithms using Proper Orthogonal Decomposition (POD) to analyze complex flow patterns from experimental datasets
            <br/ >
            Designed and constructed an interactive synthetic jet demonstration system using an ESP32 microcontroller, a signal amplifier, and a voice coil actuator, creating a hands-on educational tool to demonstrate a fluid phenomenon
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Circuit Analysis Teaching Assistant at University of Iowa"
            subtitle="Jan 2025 - May 2025"
        >
            Made answer keys for homework and exams.
            <br/ >
            Led weekly discussion sessions to review circuit analysis concepts and technics.
            <br/ >
            Made youtube videos to demonstrate LT Spice simulation and achieved 100+ views through the semester.
        </TimeLineElement>

        <TimeLineElement
            title="Differential Equation Tutor for Engineering Student Success Team at University of Iowa"
            subtitle="Aug 2024 - Feb 2025"
        >
            Guided over 500 people how to solve differential equation related problems and helped with exam prep.
        </TimeLineElement>

    </div>

    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Leadership & Involvement</div>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li><strong>IEEE:</strong> Secretary, 2025–2026 academic year; collaborated with the president to coordinate club events and support member engagement</li>
        <li><strong>ASME:</strong> Hardware Specialized Team Member; designed and supported electronic systems for team projects</li>
    </ul>


    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li><strong>Software:</strong> C, C++, Java, Python, MATLAB, Git, GitHub, Linux, WSL</li>
        <li><strong>Embedded Systems:</strong> ESP32, Arduino, Raspberry Pi, ST evaluation boards, PlatformIO, embedded communication protocols, STM32CubeIDE</li>
        <li><strong>Hardware Design & Simulation:</strong> Cadence Allegro Platform, PSpice, LTspice, KiCad, Altair Flux, Creo CAD</li>
        <li><strong>Test & Validation:</strong> LabVIEW, Simscape, Simulink, LCR/DCR meters, multimeters, oscilloscopes, transconductance amplifiers</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Relevant Coursework</div>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li><strong>Math &amp; Physics:</strong> Electromagnetic Theory, Physics I-IV, Calculus I-III, Numerical Analysis, Probability and Statistics, Discrete Math</li>
        <li><strong>Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering:</strong> Circuit Analysis, Digital Design, Electronic Instrumentation, Signals and Systems, Embedded Systems, Radio Frequency Electronics</li>
        <li><strong>Computer Science:</strong> Data Structures, Algorithms, Software Design, Object-Oriented Programming, Communication Networks, Machine Learning, Generative AI Tools</li>
    </ul>


    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Awards & Honors</div>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-2">
        <li>University Dean’s List, all semesters</li>
        <li>Electrical &amp; Computer Engineering Excellence Scholarship</li>
        <li>Best Undergraduate Poster, Mechanical Engineering Division — University of Iowa Engineering Research Open House 2025</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mb-5">
        <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Publications</div>
    </div>

    <ul class="list-disc mx-6 mb-10 grid gap-3">
        <li>
            <strong>Z. (Nomi) Wang</strong>, D. Butler, S. J. Gerlock, and C. Wang,
            “Exploring the Wild World of Vortex Shedding in a Hydrodynamics Research Laboratory,”
            <em>Synthesis: A Digital Journal of Student Science Communication</em>, 6(2), 2025.
            <a
                href="https://doi.org/10.17077/2643-8410.33922"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
                DOI: 10.17077/2643-8410.33922
            </a>
        </li>

        <li>
            S. A. Dar, C. N. Eluchie, <strong>Z. Wang</strong>, P. García-Guillén, and C. Wang,
            “Experimental Study of Novel Synthetic Jets Induced by Dynamic Deformable Surfaces,”
            <em>Proceedings of the AIAA Aviation Forum &amp; ASCEND 2025</em>,
            Las Vegas, NV, USA, July 2025, Paper AIAA 2025-3393.
            <a
                href="https://doi.org/10.2514/6.2025-3393"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
                DOI: 10.2514/6.2025-3393
            </a>
        </li>
    </ul>
